# A sort nobody reads: the list is sorted, then every later stage works one
# element at a time on its way into a sum. The ordering never reaches the
# result, so the compiler drops the sort — the hand-written Go on the other
# side is the single loop a programmer who noticed would write.
Cursed Energy: stdin
Cursed Technique: Split Text by "\n"
Channeled Energy: Convert List to Integers
Domain Expansion: Quicksort, Descending
Cursed Technique: Filter
    Using: (x) -> x % 2 = 1
Cursed Technique: Map Each
    Using: (x) -> x * 3 + 1
Maximum Technique: Sum
Reveal: stdout
